@startuml
title US10 - Register a Test Type\nClass Diagram (CD)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam classBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF9E6

class ConsoleApp {
    +registerTestType()
}

class RegisterTestType {
    -repository : TestTypeRepository&
    --
    +RegisterTestType(repository)
    +execute(internalCode, nhsCode, collectionMethodDescription) : bool
}

class TestTypeRepository {
    -testTypes : vector<TestType>
    --
    +add(testType) : bool
    +existsByInternalCode(internalCode) : bool
    +existsByNhsCode(nhsCode) : bool
}

class TestType {
    -internalCode : wstring
    -nhsCode : wstring
    -collectionMethodDescription : wstring
    --
    +TestType(internalCode, nhsCode, collectionMethodDescription)
    +getInternalCode() : const wstring&
    +getNhsCode() : const wstring&
    +getCollectionMethodDescription() : const wstring&
    +{static} isValidInternalCode(internalCode) : bool
    +{static} isValidNhsCode(nhsCode) : bool
}

ConsoleApp ..> RegisterTestType : invokes
RegisterTestType --> TestTypeRepository : uses
TestTypeRepository "1" o-- "0..*" TestType : stores

note right of TestType
The constructor enforces the official format criteria:
AC10-1: four-digit Internal Code.
AC10-2: five alphanumeric NHS Code.
end note

note bottom of TestTypeRepository
The repository checks the uniqueness criterion:
AC10-3: both codes are unique among registered test types.
end note

@enduml
